 ي","B009","root_001693","B009","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s030-0315","ي ق ن","B001","root_001696","B001","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s030-0316","ي م ن","B002","root_001698","B002","resolved_source_exact"],["a-s030-0317","ي و م","B003","root_001700","B003","resolved_source_exact"]],"review_columns":["anchor_key","source_path","line","ayah_ref","raw_excerpt"],"review_rows":[["a-s030-0001","v12/runs_11ayah/s030/full_context_control/reader_s030_a_ayah_walk.md",164,"30:15","Later-window surprise: 30:17-20 shift from the opposed destination to recurring praise, earth revived after death, and humans emerging from soil. That sequence gave `روضة` B001's watered fertility explanatory depth: the garden is not ornamental scenery attached to reward, but the fitting live environment within a larger pattern in which repaired action and divine revival produce flourishing."],["a-s030-0002","v12/runs_11ayah/s030/full_context_control/reader_s030_a_ayah_walk.md",315,"30:29","2. **Desire supplies motion but no recoverable direction.** Alongside the direct B004 sense, `ه و ي` B002 images falling toward an abyss; `ه د ي` B001 is gentle indication toward a true way, and `ض ل ل` B001 deviation from aim. The ayah moves from following to a question about guidance and then removes `ناصرين`; 30:30 answers with the command to establish one’s orientation. I infer that plural inclination behaves like descent: it can accelerate movement without furnishing a course. The absent `ن ص ر` B001, aid that makes one prevail, shows that no allied power can convert that self-authored trajectory into guidance."]]}
